WEBVTT

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.100
You aren't gonna kill me?

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.440
You aren't worth killing.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.820
My name was supposed to go 
down in history for dying here.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:18.870
If you wanna go down in history, 
do it with great deeds. Not evil ones.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:23.320
Fighting to eradicate evil <i>is</i> a great deed!

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.210
And what is evil to you?

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.760
What are your criteria?

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.010
Who is it fine to kill?

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.260
Witches and beastfallen.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.760
How many witches 
and beastfallen do you know?

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.220
Hey! Where are we going?

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.400
Follow me.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:21.990
Episode 10              Snack Time

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.500
Oh? You aren't gonna eat?

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.210
Wow! It's all gone!

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.010
Tell me, tell me. Which dish was the best?

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.260
The best...? I don't know...

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.260
They were all great.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:49.020
This soup smelled awesome.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.510
What needed work?

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.580
With the bitterness of this sauce,

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:57.530
the priest'd probably say, 
"Is there poison in this?"

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:01.860
Do you always have such good food?

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.810
On occasion, when the priest is away.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.540
Since he can't give empty compliments, 
he's a perfect taste tester!

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.240
Don't tell the others.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:15.740
It's apparently a secret that she 
practices cooking for the priest.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.150
That's right.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.550
Why did you bring me, then?

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.960
It was unbelievably tasty, right?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.800
Even though you ate with a beastfallen.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.310
Well, I mean...

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.860
Yeah...

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.690
Sh-She's a mouse?!

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.250
No way!

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.820
I ate food made by a mouse?

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.760
You sure did!

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.610
That's not nice!

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.080
Um, I'm sorry.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:54.210
You can puke it up if you're grossed out!

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.460
That would... be a waste.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:01.880
Well, thanks for the meal.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.970
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.230
Um, you don't need to apologize.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.480
Uh... It was better 
than anything I've ever eaten.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.490
Thank you for the meal.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.240
Come back again sometime!

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.990
It's pointless to try to escape.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.120
Just go to sleep.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.360
What's your name?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.130
K-Kady.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.700
I'm Kudo.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.820
That's a weird name.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.290
I'll knock your head off!

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.600
What a nice room...

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.880
I guess I ate too much.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.580
It was all a lie.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.030
Verse one, Solm!

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.780
Grant me power!

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.750
My name is Saybil!

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.430
Professor Zero taught me 
how to exert control.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.760
Wow! How do you do that?

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.050
I wanna do it, too!

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.300
I'll give it a try!

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.550
My, you can even change the shape.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.670
Hey... This is pretty hard.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:33.310
Think of it like making certain parts dark.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.060
Oh, I see.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.410
Oh! I can do it! I'm gonna get it!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.690
This is... really tough!

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.940
Even though the spell 
is simple, this is difficult.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:49.140
I should have gone to
 Professor Zero sooner.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:52.450
Too tough for thee, eh, Kudo?

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.090
Professor Los.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.370
What is it?

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.610
I'd like to get your help 
with an experiment.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:02.710
It would be dangerous with people, 
so I'd like to use the Staff of Ludens.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:04.670
Very well!

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:08.220
I am fond of the passion to improve!

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.930
I also need to say something.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.860
I am in a fine mood today. Go ahead.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:17.480
I like you.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.190
Ver—

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:26.360
A-Art thou trying to make me blush?

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.860
I adore my students as well.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.200
No. I mean, like, I want to marry you.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.060
Like, I want to be your mate.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.600
Hold on, Sayb!

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.370
Love is a negotiation!

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:42.870
You can't just push your side!

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.500
Did I do it wrong?

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:48.510
It might have been a bit... alarming...

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.490
I'm sorry, Professor Los. 
Forget this happened.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.140
How could I?!

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.640
Stand up, Kady.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:01.130
Witches are not compassionate like us.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:04.320
Everything is the fault of witches.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.740
A witch brought the north to ruin.

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.300
You all lost your families 
because of a witch.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.870
We must protect the south.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.320
Kill witches.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:30.760
Otherwise...

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.300
Kady! Kady!

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.810
Let's play!

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.370
Kady! Kady!

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.810
Let's play!

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:42.160
Kady!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.270
Come catch fish with us at the river!

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:49.320
Fish?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.000
Fishies! Fishies!

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.870
Our fondest wishie is to catch a fishie!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:57.390
I'm so excited!

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.080
We're almost at the river, everyone.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.080
Hey, face forward when you walk.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.580
Traitor...

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.740
What?

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.100
I'm amazed you can act 
all buddy-buddy with him.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:10.590
You actually trust a traitor?

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:14.600
I don't trust anybody.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.350
Including her.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:19.220
I was raised in the Church, too.

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:22.460
I'm sort of a traitor, as you put it.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.980
What're you talking about?

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:27.450
It's not easy to get people to trust you.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.820
I don't trust the Tyrant one bit, either.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.670
Earning trust is a process!

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.980
You gotta make and keep promises!

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:42.500
So, Kady, promise us you won't harm 
people who lack that power to fight.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:48.360
If you'll stick to that, 
we'll promise we won't kill you!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.650
Now, let's go!

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:56.120
I hope we catch lots of fish!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.520
Good morning, Professor Los.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.490
That's a novel way of getting up.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.530
I brought some bread.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:14.780
Would you like some?

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.890
Oh, I'll make some tea.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.810
No, no, 'tis strange!

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.160
What's going on?

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.320
Thou sure movest fast.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.660
I wanted to start my experiment ASAP.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:30.040
It's this.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:32.800
What is that? Oil?

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.180
A magic potion.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.410
A magic potion?

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:40.230
I made it based on a book 
I borrowed from Professor Zero.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.560
This book.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:48.260
The handwriting looks like 
the scratches of a strangled chicken.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.430
Oh? You can't read it?

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.820
Honestly, how canst <i>thou</i> read it?

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:57.070
The witch who wrote this has utterly 
no intention of letting others read it.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.660
Sorcerer.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:01.090
The person who wrote this book.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:05.080
It was the sorcerer Thirteen. My father.

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.580
Thou knowest about that?

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.450
Yes. I found out yesterday.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.600
That's not important, though.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.090
Not important?

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:18.770
This book describes a way 
to infuse magic into a potion.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:24.210
I thought I could apply it to make 
a potion that supplies magical energy.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.920
Thus thou needest Ludens...

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:28.850
Very well!

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.030
Well?

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.870
He seems happy.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.120
Ah, I see.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:49.330
He has more magic.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.780
About two mages' worth.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.880
Huh? That much?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.180
That's strange.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:58.250
I thought I held back quite a bit...

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.240
Maybe I need to change the ingredients...

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.390
Huh? Hey!

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.570
I'll come again.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.270
Next time, I'll try making 
several kinds of potions.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:10.390
Thou wilt? Make sure to take breaks!

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.150
{*}I will.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.900
You show concern for all of us. 
That's something I like about you.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.120
W-W-Wai—Wha?

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.650
What madest thou say that?

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:25.260
Hort said I should tell you 
my reasons for liking you.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.040
Ah, hah...

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:31.800
But then, does logic not dictate 
that thou shouldst like Hort,

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:34.290
who shows tons of concern for others?

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:35.630
True...

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:38.100
Oh, I see.

00:11:38.100 --> 00:11:42.300
I also like how you test 
people like that, Professor Los.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:50.810
When I see you grinning like, 
"I got ya there," I feel goosebumps.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.660
I like that feeling.

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:56.950
Fine. I get it!

00:11:57.930 --> 00:12:00.020
Just get going already!

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:02.220
I'll be going, then.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.200
What will you do?

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.700
I shall be monitoring the boy 
we captured yesterday.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:10.950
What? But Hort and the others said 
they're inviting him to the river.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:12.660
The river?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.350
Hey!

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:20.960
Oh, Pops.

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:23.880
I've been making the trap 
you mentioned this morning.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.470
Who said to make that?!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.540
You did, Pop—

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:32.560
Quit foolin' around makin' crap!

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:37.480
But he told me to make it.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:41.360
I don't get it.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.260
I am told you have a talent for traps.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:47.990
I have clever beasts disturbing my fields.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.440
Make me a complex trap.

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:53.540
Complex enough to keep 
a human from getting out.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:55.540
Why come to me?

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.330
I can tell from your traps that

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:01.790
you are a heartless sort.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.760
I release criminals in the forest.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.470
I tell them they'll be acquitted 
if they can escape alive.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:14.230
But since I started using 
your traps, we have had

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.480
not a single one escape.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:21.690
A frightened kid makes obvious moves.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.850
I wish to make it more interesting.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:27.230
So you want to torment them longer?

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:32.480
It's crystal clear.

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:39.960
The word is that you have 
a talent for traps.

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:41.960
Choose.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:47.380
Die here or live in agony 
that makes you pray for death.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.760
It's crystal clear.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:05.450
I caught one!

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:08.310
Look, I caught a fish, Mr. Tyrant!

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:11.030
You didn't use your trap.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.490
Because it's faster 
to grab it with my hands!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.940
These kids have so much freedom.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:17.650
They really do.

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:21.380
"Hearthful" is a northern name, isn't it?

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:23.750
Very knowledgeable of you.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:28.760
You came to a witch village even though 
a witch made your home unlivable?

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.760
Everyone asks that.

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:34.390
And how do ya answer?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:40.250
If a hunter killed one of my family 
members, I wouldn't hate all hunters.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:46.530
If a hunter killed their beloved child, 
anyone would hate the profession itself.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:52.660
In the event a hunter killed my child, 
I am sure I would become a hunter.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:58.910
And then I would think about how to hunt 
without accidentally killing children.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:01.790
That is my nature.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.400
It's how I was born and the way I was made.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.170
Ms. Hearthful, c'mere!

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.580
I'm coming.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.930
The way you were born, eh?

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.520
I see. Crystal clear.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:24.190
Did you fall for her? For the teacher?

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.560
Huh?

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:30.700
Seeing someone perfectly put together 
like that lose it and scream...

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.000
How do I put this...

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.410
It gets me worked up.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.410
I'm glad.

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:41.710
It looks like you'll be able to 
get along with everyone.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.860
Kady, come join us—

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:01.100
Kudo! Something seems wrong with Kady!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.730
Get away from him!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.410
I'm hungry.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.400
I wanna eat... I wanna eat!

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.010
Ms. Hearthful, come to the riverbank!

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.240
Mr. Tyrant!

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:44.800
Come on, Hort!

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:47.920
I'll put him to sleep!

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.480
Ravon Y Zaleik!

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:50.900
Beckon to slumber!

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.020
Chapter of Capture, verse two!

00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:54.320
Culdesomn!

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.120
Grant me power!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:58.660
My name is Hort!

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:05.920
Hungry...

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:07.640
It's not working!

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:09.330
I know!

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:12.080
I think Kady is probably unconscious!

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.430
What the hell happened to him?

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.840
A trap, I bet.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.430
What do you mean, Mr. Know-It-All?

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:26.520
That kid didn't bring just one 
Remnant of Disaster with him.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:30.620
Hort, you take the teacher 
and kids back to the village.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.950
I'll kill this thing.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:37.600
Don't be ridiculous! 
You don't have a weapon right now!

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:40.000
Leave the children to me!

00:17:41.180 --> 00:17:42.740
Come, children!

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:43.880
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.310
Impressive...

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:49.280
Hold out your arm, Tyrant. I'll heal you.

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.800
Wait, Kudo. Conserve your magic.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:58.490
Time to dig in!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:01.430
Tyrant, immobilize Kady!

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:03.060
Don't let go, even if it kills you.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.060
It's all over if Hort's 
incantation is interrupted!

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:07.640
Damn it!

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:11.820
Wherever I go, I'm never 
leaving my weapon behind again!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.950
Maelim Soh Heghans!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.320
Gather, bricks of stone!

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:24.520
Spin a net, O grass and vines!

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:29.820
Close off heaven, earth, and the four winds!

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.340
O cradle, take the transgressor 
in your embrace!

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:34.840
Chapter of Capture, verse three!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.780
Etorak!

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:39.460
Back away, Tyrant!

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.810
Grant me power!

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.620
My name is Hort!

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.600
He's sealed inside!

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.720
I want food!

00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:16.730
I want food!

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.890
Kill him, or we'll be wiped out!

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:27.450
Just hold out!

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:29.870
Once Kady's dead, I'll heal you!

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:30.890
Hort!

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:32.900
But, Kudo...

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:37.140
We'll promise we won't kill you!

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:39.870
I know.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.910
It won't just be you.

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:47.220
We'll kill him together!

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:54.470
I only have enough magic 
for one cast of Flagis.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.620
I'll go all out.

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.820
Bag Do Glaht!

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:09.180
Kalpa fire, come forth! Flare and blaze!

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:14.540
<i>You think you can take me out too
 by slowing the incantation!</i>

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:17.590
<i>It's crystal clear.</i>

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.130
Grant me power!

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:21.520
My name is Hort!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.970
Hold on, Tyrant!

00:20:35.970 --> 00:20:38.440
Chapter of Protection, final verse!

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:39.960
Quaocul!

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.590
Grant me power!

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.880
My name is Kudo!

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.280
Kudo, look!

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.610
Get up, Tyrant!

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:22.510
This ain't good. Run!

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:23.880
Run away!

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:26.560
I can't.

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:28.660
I lost too much blood.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.010
I can't run.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.270
Quit complaining and suck it up!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:36.570
If you die, we'll have 
healed you for nothing!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.150
Now stand up, old man!

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.900
You idiots.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.740
Hey! What is it?

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:58.420
Don't move! Keep your heads down!

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:03.210
Here it comes!

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.420
My dear Ludens,

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:07.790
snack time!

00:23:55.920 --> 00:23:58.940
If there were a single 
mastermind behind it all

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:09.920
<b>Next Episode  "Determination to Kill"</b>

00:23:58.940 --> 00:24:01.210
and killing them would solve everything,

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:03.460
I'd go kill 'em right now.

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:06.250
Next episode: "Determination to Kill."

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:09.230
My dear Ludens, say hello.
